# Line-ending and binary-file policy.
#
# Why this file exists: the repository used to mix conventions - main.js was
# stored with LF while index.html, manifest.json and all word lists used CRLF -
# so Git printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on almost every commit and diffs
# could be polluted by newline-only changes.
#
# `text=auto` makes Git normalise all text files to LF inside the repository
# while leaving the working tree to the platform (CRLF on Windows, LF
# elsewhere).  Nothing is rewritten until a file is next modified, so adding
# this file does not create a mass change on its own.
#
# To normalise the existing files once, in a dedicated commit:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings"
#
* text=auto

# Images and fonts are binary; never try to diff or convert them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# The Python tooling in tools/ parses main.js and wordbase/*.txt as text.
# Keeping these as plain text is intended, so be explicit about it.
*.py  text
*.txt text
*.js  text
*.json text
*.html text
*.md  text

# GitHub language detection: keep the generated bundle from dominating the
# language statistics of the repository.
main.js linguist-generated=true
wordbase/*.txt linguist-documentation
